<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  GoOuts Host — Firebase iOS configuration.

  GENERATED 6 August 2026 from lib/firebase_options.dart rather than downloaded
  from the Firebase Console. Every value below is copied from the ios block of
  that file, which flutterfire wrote when the app was registered, so the two
  cannot disagree — which is the usual way this file goes wrong.

  REVERSED_CLIENT_ID is derived from CLIENT_ID by swapping the two halves:
      289872853637-t9dd...apps.googleusercontent.com
   -> com.googleusercontent.apps.289872853637-t9dd...
  That transform was verified against driver_app's console-downloaded plist
  before being applied here.

  ── WHY THIS FILE MATTERS FOR AN APP WITH NO GOOGLE SIGN-IN ────────────────

  Flutter reads firebase_options.dart, so Firebase initialises fine without
  this file. What it is really here for is REVERSED_CLIENT_ID, which becomes
  the custom URL scheme in Info.plist. Firebase Phone Auth on iOS falls back to
  a reCAPTCHA web view whenever the silent APNs push does not arrive — on a
  simulator, with notifications denied, or on a flaky network — and that web
  view needs the scheme to hand control back to the app. Without it the OTP
  screen simply never advances.

  NOT SECRET. An iOS API key is compiled into every copy of the app and can be
  read out of any IPA. Google says as much. Security comes from Firestore rules
  and App Check, which is why this file is committed deliberately.
-->
